{
  "agents_block": "<!-- kit:studio-3d v1 begin (managed block: edit outside it) -->\n## 3D design studio: Blender, Houdini, UE5, Godot & web\n\n`project` is a 3D studio workspace for Blender, Houdini, UE5, Godot and Three.js/web.\nRead the scoped `AGENTS.md` in `dcc/blender/`, `dcc/houdini/`, `engines/ue5/`, `engines/godot/` or `web/` before working there.\n\n### Layout\n\n- `docs/`: Conventions, pipeline flows and architecture decisions.\n- `tools/`: Validation, batch export, conversion and CI scripts.\n- `refs/`: Read-only input: concept art, moodboards, photos and scans.\n- `library/`: Shared, DCC-neutral resources: HDRIs, materials, textures, kitbash, LUTs, audio.\n- `assets/`: One folder per asset in the deepest category (`assets/.../<asset_id>/`).\n- `dcc/`: Shared Blender and Houdini tooling, HDAs, lookdev scenes and templates.\n- `engines/`: Unreal Engine 5 (`engines/ue5/Studio/`) and Godot (`engines/godot/studio/`).\n- `web/`: Three.js / WebGL / WebGPU front end (`public/` assets and `src/` code).\n- `shots/`: Cinematics and shot production (`shots/<seq>/<shot>/` from `shots/_template/`).\n- `cache/`: Simulation and geometry caches only (sims, bgeo, vdb, flipbooks). Ignored.\n- `renders/`: Shot/sequence renders and playblasts (EXR sequences). Ignored by Git.\n- `deliveries/`: Versioned client and build drops. Never edit a delivered folder.\n- `.agents/`: Per-agent scratch lanes (`.agents/lanes/<agent>/`), handoffs and logs.\n- Anything that fits no folder above: ask where it goes; do not invent a new top-level folder.\n\n### Rules\n\n- Run `git lfs install` before the first commit so `.gitattributes` binaries use Git LFS.\n- One folder per asset in the deepest existing category folder (e.g. `assets/environments/modular/<asset_id>/`), copied from `assets/_template/` with `asset.yaml` filled in.\n- Per asset: editable sources in `source/<tool>/`, full-res texture sources in `textures/source/`, baked textures in `textures/baked/`, turntables/thumbnails in `preview/`, and final published files in `export/` (`fbx/`, `glb/`, `usd/`, `abc/`, `vdb/`).\n- Never put DCC source files (`.blend`, `.hip`, `.ztl`, `.spp`) in engine or web folders; assets made in Blender or Houdini arrive there as exports from the asset's `export/` folder, while engine-native assets (Blueprints, maps, materials, `.tres`, `.gdshader`) are authored in the engine.\n- The asset's `export/glb/` is the source GLB; `tools/convert/` scripts write the compressed web copy (Draco/meshopt GLB, KTX2 textures) to `web/public/models/` and `web/public/textures/`.\n- Create `Studio.uproject`, `project.godot`, `export_presets.cfg` and `package.json` with the real tool (Unreal Editor, Godot editor, or the package manager/project scaffolder), never by hand.\n- Record only verified tool versions in `TOOLS.lock`.\n- `.agents/lanes/<agent>/` is your only scratch space for files outside the engines (unreviewed Unreal assets go in `engines/ue5/Studio/Content/_Dev/`); put handoff notes in `.agents/handoff/`.\n<!-- kit:studio-3d end -->\n",
